      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Oct 07 2020 19:38:13 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Minimizing scarring for a psychological and emotional recovery</span></span></p>\n<p>While some may see their scars as an empowering symbol, many do not. In fact, 87%<br>\nof women are self-conscious due to scars from breast cancer surgery.<sup>3</sup> There are a number of surgical options available, including oncoplastic surgery techniques, an advanced surgical approach in which breast surgeons remove cancerous tissue through a single incision made in inconspicuous areas to minimize visible scarring. Surgeons can use oncoplastic techniques in either a mastectomy or lumpectomy procedure. Through thermally-cool, volumetric illumination, our Illuminated Instruments provide surgeons with enhanced visualization that offer positive physical and psychosocial wellbeing for patients by providing oncologic outcomes equal to traditional techniques.<sup>4</sup></p>\n<p>Meet Dr. Anne Peled, an oncoplastic surgeon. On the day she was getting ready to perform a double mastectomy and breast reconstruction, her phone rang and she learned that the disease she spent her life treating had found her. “I had to remind myself what I tell my patients,” she said. “That this is very treatable and, in many cases, curable.”<br>\n<br>\nDr. Peled was able to put together an amazing team of caring and talented clinicians. She got through treatment smoothly and relatively easily, thanks, in part, to the type of hidden scar surgery she performs on her own patients. And today, she speaks with every patient with a unique level of shared understanding.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 13 2020 18:44:36 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
